7,1387,1444,1702,1725,1734,1840,1847} with only 1-2 incidental extras. No old contact set is retired and no new one recruited. Controls rule out alternatives: the roster nodes are steadily active across all epochs with modest degree, so the overlap is not hub-popularity driven; and high raw volume plus near-zero triangle structure show that volume and time-ignored connectivity carry no signal here. The turnover is in which group member transmits, not in whom the group contacts, so an abrupt partner regime switch is absent."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Group activity is high and roughly steady** (step_01, step_02, step_03): ~90\u201394 events per member over the window, ~120 group events per 3000-time bin with no collapse or burst \u2014 no volume discontinuity.\n\n**Members activate sequentially, not simultaneously** (step_11, step_12, step_13, step_14):\n- 323/477/865/889 \u2192 active only in [246, 10246]\n- 1039 \u2192 straddles ~[8246, 12246]; 1119/1389/1432 \u2192 [10246, 20246]\n- 1530/1553/1639/1776 \u2192 [20246, 30246]\n\nThis looks like a change point at first glance. But the decisive test is the **contact sets**, not the activity timing.\n\n**The partner set is invariant across every epoch** (steps 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 21, 23, 24, 25, 26, 27, 28, 32): every member, in every sub-window, contacts the identical ~30-node roster {39, 55, 68, 118, 139, 306, 337, 425, 441, 585, 722, 788, 794, 901, 955, 977, 1008, 1009, 1057, 1145, 1147, 1181, 1247, 1387, 1444, 1702, 1725, 1734, 1840, 1847}, plus at most 1\u20132 idiosyncratic extras (1957, 1635/1836, 1139, 1076, 227, 440/453).\n\nApplying the prescribed test at candidate change point t\u224810246 with half-window 5000: contacts in [5246,10246] (step_23) vs [10246,15246] (step_24) are **the same 30 nodes \u2014 Jaccard \u2248 1.0, zero old-set retirement, zero new-set recruitment.**\n\n**Confounder controls:** the roster nodes are themselves persistently active across all six 5000-unit epochs (step_30: 72/75/44/62/66/68 events) with modest individual degrees (step_31), so the constant overlap is not a \"hub popularity\" artifact. Step_22 confirms the group's raw volume is high (a volume-only heuristic would fire) and step_29 shows near-zero triangle structure, so neither volume nor static connectivity carries the signal.\n\n**Conclusion:** what turns over is *which group member is transmitting*, not *whom the group talks to*. There is no old-contacts-to-new-contacts substitution.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8b4a3bfa\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [323, 477, 865, 889, 1039, 1119, 1389, 1432, 1530, 1553, 1639, 1776],\n  \"window\": [246, 30246],\n  \"confidence\": 0.79,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_23\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_24\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_18\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_21\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_25\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_26\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_27\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_28\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_32\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_30\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_31\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_22\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"